        "answer": {
          "short": "Collinear; both gradients are $-\\frac{2}{3}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}m_{AB}&=\\frac{3-5}{1-(-2)}\\\\m_{AB}&=-\\frac{2}{3}\\\\m_{BC}&=\\frac{-1-3}{7-1}\\\\m_{BC}&=-\\frac{4}{6}\\\\m_{BC}&=-\\frac{2}{3}\\end{align*}$$\nThe gradients are equal, so the points are collinear.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 8
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$P(-2,7),\\ Q(1,1),\\ R(4,-6)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Not collinear; the gradients are $-2$ and $-\\frac{7}{3}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}m_{PQ}&=\\frac{1-7}{1-(-2)}\\\\m_{PQ}&=\\frac{-6}{3}\\\\m_{PQ}&=-2\\\\m_{QR}&=\\frac{-6-1}{4-1}\\\\m_{QR}&=-\\frac{7}{3}\\end{align*}$$\nThe gradients are different, so the points are not collinear.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$P(-5,-4),\\ Q(-2,-2),\\ R(1,0)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Collinear; both gradients are $\\frac{2}{3}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}m_{PQ}&=\\frac{-2-(-4)}{-2-(-5)}\\\\m_{PQ}&=\\frac{2}{3}\\\\m_{QR}&=\\frac{0-(-2)}{1-(-2)}\\\\m_{QR}&=\\frac{2}{3}\\end{align*}$$\nThe gradients are equal, so the points are collinear.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
